Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 28 08:45:01 2026 +1100

    hacking: Add N351 for config reads at import time
    
    N351 reports a cfg.CONF option read outside any function. Such a read
    runs at import, so any process that imports the module before parsing
    its configuration sees the default. The ovsdb manager options and the
    three sites fixed in the previous change were all found by hand.
    
    The check follows "def" lines rather than the indent, so reads inside
    module-level blocks such as "try:" and class bodies are caught too,
    while reads in a lambda or behind register_opts and friends are not.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    Change-Id: Idda61a65682799d796bee649e785ca180b9ca9f0
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

